      "text": "To solve the expression \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we can substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression and then simplify.\n\nStarting with the expression:\n\\[\n(2x + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(x = 3\\):\n\\[\n(2(3) + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nNext, perform the multiplication inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n(6 + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nThen, perform the addition inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n11^2\n\\]\n\nFinally, compute the square of 11:\n\\[\n11^2 = 121\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
